# Vector — one-command self-hosted stack. Copy to `.env` and edit.
#   cp .env.example .env
#   ./bootstrap.sh        # downloads raw data, builds graph/tiles/index, generates secrets
#   docker compose up -d  # brings up the whole stack; open http://localhost:8088
#
# NEVER commit .env. Every value below is either a region parameter or a
# secret that bootstrap.sh regenerates randomly on first run if you leave it
# as the placeholder below. bootstrap.sh refuses to boot with a demo/default
# secret unless VECTOR_DEV=1.

# -- Region parameter (this is what lets coverage grow past Doha) -------------
# Identifier used for file names and the OSRM graph. Must match VECTOR_PBF_URL.
VECTOR_REGION=qatar

# URL + bbox for the OSM/Overpass extract for VECTOR_REGION. bootstrap.sh uses
# VECTOR_PBF_URL to download the raw data; VECTOR_BBOX bounds the query.
VECTOR_PBF_URL=https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter
VECTOR_BBOX=24.4,50.7,26.2,51.8

# --- secrets (bootstrap.sh generates random values on first run) -------------
# A boot refuses to proceed with the demo defaults unless VECTOR_DEV=1.
VECTOR_SERVICE_TOKEN=__GENERATE__
VECTOR_WEB_TOKEN=__GENERATE__
VECTOR_PG_USER=vector
VECTOR_PG_PASSWORD=__GENERATE__

# Set to 1 ONLY for local dev where the demo tokens are acceptable:
VECTOR_DEV=0

# --- public origin (only needed for a cross-origin / packaged client) --------
# The origin(s) this deployment is reachable at from a browser, space-separated.
# Leave EMPTY for a purely local stack: the viewer is same-origin and the
# default CSP (connect-src 'self') is already correct.
#
# Set it when a packaged client calls this host. Inside a Capacitor WebView the
# page origin is the webview's own scheme (capacitor:// or http://localhost),
# never the public host, so every API/tile/glyph fetch is cross-origin. CORS and
# CSP are INDEPENDENT gates: opening CORS at the proxy while connect-src stays
# 'self' still blocks the fetch in the browser, and the symptom is a blank map
# with every endpoint returning 200.
# Must be scheme://host[:port] — no trailing path, no wildcard.
# VECTOR_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://your-host.example.com

# --- the self-evolving loop (issues 05-10, adr-0065 / adr-0066) --------------
# Every path below has a working default; set them only to move data elsewhere.
# The whole loop is driven by one scheduled command:
#
#     node scripts/run-evolution-cycle.mjs
#
# which runs vacuum -> aggregate -> promote -> re-bake tiles -> metrics ->
# dashboard, and renders "is the map improving?" at http://localhost:8088/evolution
#
# Nothing here needs to be set for the map to work. With no traces collected,
# every stage reports "skipped" and the dashboard honestly says nothing has been
# measured yet.

# S2 quarantine store (72 h TTL, adr-0065). Location data lives here and nowhere
# else, and it is never what persists.
# VECTOR_TRACE_DB=vector-web/data/traces.db

# S4 durable learned facts. Non-personal by construction: aggregates that have
# already cleared the K=5 floor.
# VECTOR_FACTS_DB=vector-learning/learning-data/facts.db
# VECTOR_WATERMARK=vector-learning/learning-data/watermark.json

# The routable network the batch job map-matches against, and the tiles a
# geometry promotion re-bakes.
# VECTOR_ROADS_GEOJSON=vector-osrm/data/qatar.geojson
# VECTOR_TILES_DIR=vector-tile-server/tiles
# VECTOR_REBAKE_ZOOMS=12,13,14,15,16

# S5 promotion exports — one file per consumer, read over the filesystem rather
# than in-process (adr-0003).
# VECTOR_PROMOTED_DIR=vector-learning/learning-data/promoted

# Consumers. Each is opt-in: unset means that service behaves exactly as it did
# before anything was learned.
# VECTOR_LEARNED_FACTS=vector-learning/learning-data/promoted/learned_speed.json  # -> vector-routing
# VECTOR_LEARNED_POIS=vector-learning/learning-data/promoted/learned_pois.json    # -> vector-geocoder
# VECTOR_ETA_LOG=vector-web/data/eta.jsonl                                        # -> vector-routing

# The one-flag rollback (adr-0066). Set to 0 and routing + the geocoder are
# byte-for-byte their pre-learning selves; the base graph and OSM index were
# never mutated, so there is nothing to undo.
# VECTOR_LEARNED_ENABLED=1

# --- time bands for learned speed profiles (adr-0067) -----------------------
# Evidence is bucketed per (segment, time band), and bands are evaluated in the
# LOCAL civil time of the region you are mapping — traffic follows local clocks
# and local working weeks, not UTC. Defaults are Qatar.
#
# These MUST be identical for vector-learning and vector-routing: the band
# definition is duplicated across the two repos (adr-0003 forbids the import), and
# a drift silently applies the wrong time-of-week's speeds.
#
# Changing either value re-keys every speed_profile fact. Run
#   python -m vector_learning retire-stale-facts --facts <facts.db>
# afterwards, or the old-keyed facts stay active, get promoted, and are silently
# skipped by the router while the dashboard reports coverage it does not have.
# VECTOR_WEEK_UTC_OFFSET_H=3
# VECTOR_WEEKEND_DAYS=4,5      # Monday=0; Qatar weekend is Friday(4), Saturday(5)

# Issue 10 dashboard + privacy counters.
# VECTOR_EVOLUTION_DIR=vector-web/data
# VECTOR_EVOLUTION_HISTORY=90
# VECTOR_PRIVACY_COUNTERS=vector-web/data/privacy_counters.json
# --- RevenueCat (client SDK keys; public by design, still not committed) -----
# Test Store key for debug builds; Play public key for releases. Pass to Gradle
# as -PrevenueCatKey=. Leave empty for a self-hosted build with no paid tier.
REVENUECAT_TEST_KEY=
REVENUECAT_PLAY_KEY=
